      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're dealing with what sounds like a low-level, persistent form of workplace mischief, and you need to frame it in a way that management takes seriously. Don't just say \"it feels targeted\"; instead, document the *pattern* of the disruptions, like noting which specific aisles or types of inventory are being affected. You could categorize these incidents as \"micro-disruptions\" or \"inventory integrity anomalies\" rather than just \"annoyances.\" Presenting data—even just a log of the occurrences—is the best way to move this from a \"paranoid\" feeling to a measurable operational issue.",
      "source": "target",
